description: "You can't go wrong serving this easy chef's salad, prepared with grilled chicken breast and a creamy black pepper ranch dressing, for lunch or dinner!"
---

> Time: PT70M

= Ingredients

@skinless, boneless chicken breast halves{1 7/8%pounds}\
@kosher salt, divided{1 1/4%teaspoon}\
@whole buttermilk{5/16%cup}\
@mayonnaise{5/16%cup}\
@sour cream{5/16%cup}\
@chopped fresh chives{1 7/8%teaspoons}\
@chopped fresh parsley{1 7/8%teaspoons}\
@chopped fresh dill{1 7/8%teaspoons}\
@ground black pepper{1 7/8%teaspoons}\
@grated or minced garlic{5/16%teaspoon}\
@butter lettuce, torn{6 1/4%ounces}\
@chopped iceberg lettuce{3 3/4%cups}\
@thinly sliced English cucumber{1 1/4%cup}\
@sharp Cheddar cheese, cut into 1/2-inch cubes{5%ounces}\
@pint cherry tomatoes, halved{1 1/4}\
@medium avocado - peeled, pitted, and sliced{1 1/4}\
@large hard-boiled eggs, peeled and quartered{2 1/2}

= Directions
Preheat a gas grill to medium heat (400 to 450 degrees F, or 200 to 230 degrees C) or a grill pan over medium-high heat; oil the grates. Pat chicken dry and sprinkle evenly with 3/4 teaspoon salt.

Place chicken on the preheated grill and cook, turning occasionally, until a thermometer inserted into the thickest part registers 165 degrees F (74 degrees C), about 15 minutes. Transfer to a cutting board and let rest for 10 minutes before chopping.

While chicken rests, stir together buttermilk, mayonnaise, sour cream, chives, parsley, dill, black pepper, garlic, and remaining 1/4 teaspoon of the salt in a medium bowl.

Toss butter lettuce and iceberg in a large bowl or platter. Arrange chicken, cucumber, cheese, tomatoes, avocado, and eggs over lettuce. Drizzle 1/2 of the dressing. Serve with remaining dressing on the side.
